error[ffi_constant_type]: `PAINTED_SHADE` in `fixedbugs-094-values.h` cannot be a `Painted`: clang refuses the header's value at line 19: implicit conversion from enumeration type 'enum shade' to different enumeration type 'enum colour'
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-094-a-value-of-another-kind-than-its-field-is-told.hero:13:5
     |
  13 |     constant PAINTED_SHADE: Painted  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-094-values.h` line 19 reads `#define PAINTED_SHADE {DARK, 2}`
  note: C only warns of this, and the accessor that builds a record's constant makes it an error: the value C would build is not the one the header wrote, or is of another kind than the field it fills
  note: a group's `constant` of a record is the value C builds when it initialises the header's `struct painted` with `PAINTED_SHADE` (§ 13): declare it at the record whose value the header spells, or name the header that spells `PAINTED_SHADE` for `struct painted`
